---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import PromptOptimizer from '../../components/PromptOptimizer.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Prompt Length Optimizer" description="Scan a prompt for filler phrases and get token/sentence-length stats to help tighten it up.">
  <PromptOptimizer client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why trim prompts</h2>
  <p>Shorter, more direct prompts reduce token cost and often produce more focused outputs — filler phrases add length without adding instruction clarity.</p>

  <h2>Common Prompt Trimming Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cutting necessary context to save tokens</strong>, sacrificing clarity the model actually needs to produce a good response.</li>
    <li><strong>Not testing trimmed prompts against real outputs</strong>, assuming shorter automatically means equally effective without verifying.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Prompt Optimizer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Trimming a verbose prompt before deploying it at scale to reduce cost</li>
    <li>Reviewing a team's prompt templates for unnecessary filler language</li>
    <li>Learning to write more direct, effective prompts</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
